🫲
"Conductor"/en
=== start/en
¶Conduct the Imperial March with your hands. No keyboard, no buttons — the
camera watches one hand and the whole orchestra answers, and a fleet crosses
the screen for as long as the music is going.

Every instruction is printed on the stage, so you can learn it without
reading this.¶

hand: Hand()
¶The hand a moment ago, which is how a gesture that is a *movement* — closing
a fist, circling a palm — can be told from one that is just a shape.¶
before: ← 1 hand

¶Every shape the orchestra listens for, as one word. Order matters: a tucked
fist and a thumbs-up both have four fingers down, so the tucked one is tested
first, when the thumb is down too.¶
ƒ shape(g•Gesture|ø)•''
	g•ø ? 'none'
	(~g.index & ~g.middle & ~g.ring & ~g.pinky & ~g.thumb) ? 'tucked'
	(g.thumb & ~g.index & ~g.middle & ~g.ring & ~g.pinky) ? 'thumb'
	(g.index & ~g.middle & ~g.ring & ~g.pinky & ~g.thumb) ? 'one'
	(g.index & g.middle & ~g.ring & ~g.pinky & ~g.thumb) ? 'two'
	(g.index & g.middle & g.ring & ~g.pinky & ~g.thumb) ? 'three'
	(g.index & g.middle & g.ring & g.pinky & ~g.thumb) ? 'four'
	g.open ? 'open'
	'none'

now: shape(hand)
was: shape(before)

¶A gesture held still would fire every frame, so only a *change* counts as a
command. This is the whole trick that makes holding a shape safe.¶
fresh: (now = was) ? 'none' now

¶Closing an open palm into a fist. A movement, not a shape, so it needs both
frames: palm open then, fingers down now.¶
closing: (was = 'open') & ((now = 'tucked') | (now = 'thumb'))

¶Circling counterclockwise. The cross product of where the hand was and where
it is turns positive when it sweeps counterclockwise about the centre, so
adding that up while the palm is open finds a circle without ever needing to
know where the circle's middle is. It leaks away when the hand stops, so a
stray flick never adds up to a command.¶
ƒ sweep(g•Gesture|ø h•Gesture|ø)•#m^2
	g•ø ? 0m^2
		h•ø ? 0m^2
			((h.place.x · g.place.y) - (h.place.y · g.place.x))

swirl•#m^2: 0m^2 … ∆ hand …
	(now = 'open') ? ((swirl · 0.85) + sweep(hand before)) 0m^2

circling: swirl > 0.6m^2

¶What the orchestra is doing. Paused keeps the music on stage at silent
volume, so it holds its place and picking it up again carries on; stopped
takes it off, so starting again begins from the top.¶
state: 'stopped' … ∆ hand …
	closing ? 'paused'
	(fresh = 'tucked') ? 'stopped'
	(fresh = 'thumb') ? 'playing'
	((state = 'paused') & circling) ? 'playing'
	state

¶Which section is playing, and what plays it.¶
section: 1 … ∆ hand …
	(fresh = 'one') ? ((section - 1).max(1))
	(fresh = 'two') ? ((section + 1).min(2))
	section

instrument•🔈: 🔈.🎹 … ∆ hand …
	(fresh = 'three') ? 🔈.🎹
	(fresh = 'four') ? 🔈.🎸
	instrument

¶Height is loudness and sideways is key, both read straight off the hand
rather than remembered, so they follow it continuously.¶
lift: ((hand.place.y + 3m) ÷ 6m).min(1).max(0)
loudness: 100% · lift
shift: 12semitones · ((hand.place.x ÷ 8m).min(0.5).max(-0.5))

¶The Imperial March, all eight bars. It's written on a chromatic scale so its
out-of-key notes — the flat second, and the chromatic slide in the second
half — can be written at all. Degree 1 is the low E♭ and every step up is one
semitone, so the numbers here are intervals rather than scale steps.¶
march: [
	5 ø ø ø 5 ø ø ø 5 ø ø ø 1 ø ø 8
	5 ø ø ø 1 ø ø 8 5 ø ø ø ø ø ø ø
	12 ø ø ø 12 ø ø ø 12 ø ø ø 13 ø ø 8
	4 ø ø ø 1 ø ø 8 5 ø ø ø ø ø ø ø
	17 ø ø ø 5 ø ø 5 17 ø ø ø 16 ø ø 15
	14 13 14 ø ø ø 6 ø 11 ø ø ø 9 ø ø 8
	7 6 7 ø ø ø 1 ø 4 ø ø ø 1 ø ø 4
	8 ø ø ø 5 ø ø 8 12 ø ø ø ø ø ø ø
]

¶The answering phrase, the same shape an octave and a half up.¶
bridge: [
	20 ø ø ø 20 ø ø ø 20 ø ø ø 16 ø ø 23
	20 ø ø ø 16 ø ø 23 20 ø ø ø ø ø ø ø
]

¶A root under it, an octave down — the track carries its own key, so the bass
moves with the conducting hand along with everything else.¶
bass: [
	5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø
	5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø
]

tune: (section = 1) ? march bridge
low: (section = 1) ? bass [5 ø 5 ø 5 ø 5 ø]

¶How far the fleet has travelled. It counts its own ticks rather than reading
the clock, so the ships hang still the moment the music pauses or stops.¶
travel: 0 … ∆ Time(40ms) … (state = 'playing') ? (travel + 1) travel

ƒ label()•''
	(state = 'playing') ? '▶'
	(state = 'paused') ? '⏸'
	'⏹'

ƒ status()•''
	(state = 'playing') ? 'section \section\ of 2'
	(state = 'paused') ? 'paused — circle an open palm counterclockwise'
	'show a 👍 to begin'

¶One line of the instructions, dim so the music and the fleet read first.¶
ƒ line(text•'')•Phrase Phrase(text 0.4m color: Color(70% 6 250°))

¶A ship crossing the stage. Its lane sets how high it flies and how far along
it starts, so they never fly in formation.¶
ƒ ship(icon•'' lane•# speed•#)•Phrase
	Phrase(
		icon
		1.3m
		place: Place(
			(((((travel · speed) + (lane · 47)) % 200) - 100) · 0.09) · 1m
			((lane · 1.7) - 2.6) · 1m
		)
	)

fleet: [
	ship('🛸' 0 3)
	ship('🚀' 1 2)
	ship('🛰️' 2 4)
	ship('🛸' 3 5)
]

display: 🔳(
	Stack(padding: 0.26m)
	[
		💬(label() 2m)
		💬(status() 0.55m)
		line('👍 thumb up — start')
		line('open palm, then close it into a fist — pause')
		line('fist with the thumb tucked in — stop')
		line('open palm circled counterclockwise — resume')
		line('hand higher or lower — louder or quieter')
		line('hand left or right — lower or raise the key')
		line('☝ back a section     ✌ forward a section')
		line('🤟 piano     🖖 guitar')
	]
)

song: 🎼(
	[
		🎶(tune instrument: instrument beat: 0.25beats)
		🎶(low instrument: 🔈.drums beat: 1beats key: -12semitones volume: 85%)
	]
	tempo: 108beats/min
	scale: 🎼.chromatic
	key: shift
	volume: (state = 'paused') ? 0% loudness
	name: 'imperial \section\'
)

¶Stopped takes the music off the stage entirely, which is what makes starting
again begin from the top. A Stage's content can't hold ø, so the list itself
is what changes.¶
🎭(
	(state = 'stopped')
		? [:fleet display]
		[:fleet display song]
	background: Color(10% 8 260°)
	color: Color(94% 0 0°)
)
